  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shiv Parsan Yadav vs The State Of Bihar on 27 March, 2024 Author: Prabhat Kumar Singh Bench: Prabhat Kumar Singh In The High Court Of Judicature At Patna Criminal Miscellaneous No.11851 of 2024 Arising Out of Ps. Case No.-118 Year-2016 Thana- Sathi District- Wes ====================================================== Shiv Parsan Yadav S/o Dhruv Yadav Resident of Village-Basantpur, P.S.-Sathi, District-West Champaran. ... . Versus The State of Bihar Bihar ... ... Opposite Party/s ====================================================== Appearance : For the Petitioner/s : Mr.Dhananjay Kumar For the Opposite Party/s : Mr.Ashok Kumar Singh ====================================================== Coram: Honourable Mr. Justice Prabhat Kumar Singh Oral Order Shiv Parsan Yadav vs The State Of Bihar on 27 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/161828650/ 1 4.",
    "facts": "2. Petitioner seeks regular bail in a case registered under Sections 147, 148, 149, 341, 323,324, 302 and 504 of the Indian Penal Code and Section 27 of the Arms Act. Thereafter, he himself fired through his gun at the father of the informant causing firearm injury on his leg and co- Patna High Court CR. MISC. Both of them rushed to the hospital but they died in course of treatment.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the specific allegation of causing firearm injury to the uncle and father of the informant is against co-accused Dhruv Yadav and Rajendra Yadav. So far petitioner is concerned, there is general and omnibus allegation of assault by means of lathi, farsa and no specific overt act has been alleged against him. He further submits that in post-mortem report of the dead body of both the deceased, only one lacerated injury caused by hard and blunt substance was found on the person of father of the informant, whereas two lacerated injuries caused by hard and blunt substance were found on the person of uncle of the informant. It is also submitted that the petitioner was not present at the time of the occurrence rather he was staying in Patna High Court CR. MISC. No.11851 of 2024(3) dt.27-03-2024 other State for earning livelihood."
  },
